    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`shipping_cost` is now implemented in `solution.py`, and the 22 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't run a coverage report, so the 90% gate is unconfirmed. The tests exercise every branch, so I expect it to clear.\n\nThe code follows the spec rules in order. Billable weight is the larger of actual and volumetric weight, rounded up to the next half kilogram. Base charge, zone factor, free shipping, the 12.00 oversize surcharge and final `ROUND_HALF_UP` rounding all follow the spec. Floats are converted through `str()`.\n\nOne choice the spec doesn't cover: NaN or infinite inputs raise `ValueError`.\n\nThe tests cover the base-charge examples, volumetric weight, zone factors, the free-shipping threshold, the oversize surcharge and rounding. They also check that bad types raise `TypeError` and bad values or zones raise `ValueError`.",
